.TH OPCCHECK 1 "January 2024" "opccheck 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
opccheck \- OPC-DA security checker for industrial control systems
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B opccheck
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fITARGET\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B opccheck
is a command-line tool for security assessment of OPC-DA (OLE for Process Control \- Data Access) servers.
It performs various security checks including DCOM connectivity tests, authentication verification, and browsing capability assessment.
.PP
OPC-DA is widely used in industrial control systems (ICS), SCADA systems, and manufacturing environments.
This tool helps identify security misconfigurations that could expose industrial systems to unauthorized access.
.PP
The tool is designed to work on Linux and macOS systems, implementing DCOM/RPC protocol handling without requiring Windows dependencies.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS "Target Specification"
.TP
.I TARGET
The target OPC-DA server specified as a hostname, DNS name, or IP address.
.SS "Port Scanning Options"
.TP
.B \-\-scan\-ports
Scan for accessible DCOM ports. This is enabled by default.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-port\-scan
Disable port scanning.
.TP
.BI \-\-port\-range " START-END"
Specify a custom port range to scan (e.g., 49152-49200).
.TP
.B \-\-common\-ports\-only
Only scan commonly used DCOM ports. This is the default behavior.
.TP
.BI \-p " PORT" "\fR,\fP \-\-port " PORT
Check a specific port only.
.SS "Security Check Options"
.TP
.B \-\-check\-auth
Check authentication requirements for OPC-DA connections. Enabled by default.
.TP
.B \-\-check\-browse
Check if OPC item browsing is possible. Enabled by default.
.TP
.B \-\-check\-activation
Check if DCOM remote activation is enabled. Enabled by default.
.SS "Output Options"
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Enable verbose output with detailed information about each check.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Quiet mode \- only display security findings.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Output results in JSON format for integration with other tools.
.TP
.BI \-o " FILE" "\fR,\fP \-\-output " FILE
Write results to the specified file in JSON format.
.SS "Connection Options"
.TP
.BI \-t " SECONDS" "\fR,\fP \-\-timeout " SECONDS
Set connection timeout in seconds. Default is 5 seconds.
.SS "General Options"
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Display version information and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display help message and exit.
.SH SECURITY CHECKS
.B opccheck
performs the following security assessments:
.SS "1. DCOM Port Accessibility"
Scans for accessible DCOM ports including:
.IP \(bu 2
Port 135 (RPC Endpoint Mapper)
.IP \(bu 2
Port 139 (NetBIOS)
.IP \(bu 2
Port 445 (SMB)
.IP \(bu 2
Port 593 (HTTP RPC Endpoint Mapper)
.IP \(bu 2
Legacy dynamic ports (1024-1030)
.IP \(bu 2
Modern dynamic ports (49152-49160)
.SS "2. RPC Endpoint Mapper"
Verifies if the RPC Endpoint Mapper is accessible, which can reveal information about available DCOM services.
.SS "3. OPC-DA Authentication"
Tests whether the OPC-DA server allows unauthenticated or anonymous connections.
.SS "4. OPC Item Browsing"
Checks if clients can browse OPC items through the IOPCBrowseServerAddressSpace interface.
.SS "5. DCOM Remote Activation"
Determines if DCOM remote activation is enabled via the OXID Resolver and IRemUnknown interfaces.
.SS "6. OPC Server Enumeration"
Tests accessibility of the IOPCServerList interface for enumerating OPC servers.
.SH SEVERITY LEVELS
Results are classified by severity:
.TP
.B CRITICAL
Issues requiring immediate attention. Anonymous access or critical misconfigurations.
.TP
.B HIGH
Significant security concerns that should be addressed promptly.
.TP
.B MEDIUM
Moderate security issues that increase attack surface.
.TP
.B LOW
Minor security concerns or best practice violations.
.TP
.B INFO
Informational findings with no direct security impact.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
No critical or high severity issues found.
.TP
.B 1
High severity issues found.
.TP
.B 2
Critical severity issues found.
.TP
.B 130
Operation interrupted by user (Ctrl+C).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Basic security check:
.B opccheck 192.168.1.100
.TP
Verbose check with DNS hostname:
.B opccheck opcserver.example.com \-v
.TP
Extended port scan with custom range:
.B opccheck 10.0.0.50 \-\-port\-range 49152-49200
.TP
Skip port scanning:
.B opccheck 192.168.1.100 \-\-no\-port\-scan
.TP
Extended timeout for slow networks:
.B opccheck server.local \-\-timeout 10
.TP
JSON output:
.B opccheck 192.168.1.100 \-\-json
.TP
Save results to file:
.B opccheck 192.168.1.100 \-o results.json
.TP
Check specific port:
.B opccheck 192.168.1.100 \-p 135
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/local/bin/opccheck
Default installation location.
.TP
.I ~/.opccheck/config
User configuration file (optional, not yet implemented).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B OPCCHECK_TIMEOUT
Default timeout value in seconds. Overridden by \-\-timeout option.
.SH SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS
.B Important:
This tool is intended for authorized security testing and research only.
Always obtain proper authorization before testing systems you do not own.
.PP
Recommended use cases include:
.IP \(bu 2
Security assessments of industrial control systems
.IP \(bu 2
Authorized penetration testing of OPC infrastructure
.IP \(bu 2
Compliance verification for OPC-DA deployments
.IP \(bu 2
Network security audits
.IP \(bu 2
Vulnerability assessments
